# 00 — THE OBJECTIVE

The existing WORLD SIGNAL frontend has a strong functional foundation and an established editorial design system.

The purpose of this phase is to improve the quality of the complete visual experience.

I want the interface to become:

- More elegant.
- More visually attractive.
- More sophisticated.
- More expressive.
- More cohesive.
- More detailed.
- More enjoyable to read.
- More memorable.

This is a high-fidelity editorial craftsmanship phase.

It is NOT a functionality expansion phase.

It is NOT a complete rewrite.

It is NOT a generic redesign exercise.

The current design already includes valuable work: editorial cover plates, original illustrations, verified media, custom typography, asymmetric story layouts, relationship visualization, detailed evidence tables, and reader utilities.

Preserve those foundations.

Improve the way they work together.

The final product should feel like a carefully art-directed international affairs magazine combined with a modern visual journalism publication.

**I want visual sophistication, not visual noise.**

Every improvement should make the experience more beautiful, readable, meaningful, and coherent.

